# longrun model map

Strong model for the lead and for judging: these roles decide.
Fast model for writing and finding: these roles produce volume.
Checkers run on a different model family from the writers they check, so they do not share blind spots.

| Role | Model | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| lead | <<FILL: strong model, e.g. your best reasoning model>> | one long chat; decides, briefs, merges |
| writer | <<FILL: fast model>> | many short runs; does the work |
| finder | <<FILL: fast model>> | reads and reports file pointers |
| checker | <<FILL: strong model, different family from the writer>> | measures; passes or rejects |
| live-check | <<FILL: model, different family from the writer>> | opens the live result as a user would |

When you spawn a worker with the Task tool, set its model from this table. Never give a checker the writer's model family.
